// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// Explicit derive that runs (issue #53 Scope B; ADR 0058): the module home of
// `derive_hash`, the derive that turns a struct value into a number the two
// backends agree on. Nothing else is declared here yet: the derive is a
// bodiless generic declaration lowered per concrete `Type` at the call site,
// never a metadata blob -- decl-listing its body would only add a name both
// backends must special-case, one more thing to drift.
//
// THE DERIVE. `derive_hash(v)` mixes a struct value's fields in declaration
// order with FNV-1a 64:
//   h = 14695981039346656037;
//   for each byte of each field's value, least-significant byte first:
//     h = (h ^ byte) * 1099511628211  (mod 2^64)
// It is never a byte blit of the whole object: padding never enters the mix
// (two representations with the same field values always hash the same) and a
// layout-model change -- a field moved, a width widened -- shows up in the
// number, exactly as such a change should.
//
// WHAT EACH FIELD CONTRIBUTES.
//   * An integer scalar mixes its two's-complement bytes zero-extended to 64
//     bits first (int is 4 bytes, long 8, bool and char 1); the extension
//     only pads, because the mixer reads no more bytes than the field's own
//     width. `int` -1's four bytes are ff ff ff ff exactly like the `uint`
//     clamp, and -1 stored into a long is ff ff ff ff ff ff ff ff.
//   * float and double mix their IEEE bit patterns (4 and 8 bytes).
//   * A nested struct recurses with its own fields; an empty struct adds
//     nothing, so the sole hash of `{}` is the FNV offset basis,
//     14695981039346656037.
//   * A payloadless enum field mixes its tag word as the `int` it is
//     (reflect.fin's model: a payloadless enum is its tag).
//
// BOUNDARIES, STATED SO A CALLER IS NOT SURPRISED BY A REFUSAL: a field of
// type `string`, an array, a pointer, a nullable, an interface reference,
// a payloaded enum (bare or instantiated), a `fn`-typed field or a struct
// nested more than sixteen deep refuses naming the field and the kind --
// each of those needs its own measured walk before this derive lowers it
// rather than guesses at one (backend invariant: a refusal names the
// construct and the gap; the stage walks generic instances under its own
// recorded boundary, the C++ walks them). The value argument binds through
// its type spelling, so a plain value spelling (`p`, `q`) lowers while an
// exotic argument falls through to the old path, which refuses on its own.
// These have their own tests (Soundness_Derive in tests/test_soundness.cpp).
//
// The `Type` parameter is not spelled at most call sites: `derive_hash(p)`
// with `p` a Point binds through the VALUE argument on both backends (the
// monomorphization the phase-B plan promised for wrappers bound this way;
// `@type_size(T)` inside one erased body still refuses on the stage, which
// keeps one body -- reflect.fin records that door separately). The spelling
// lives on hash_word's footing (lib/std/hashmap.fin:107): a bodiless generic
// declaration, lowered per concrete `T` by each backend at the call site.

pub fun derive_hash<Type>(x: Type) <ulong>;

namespace std {

}
